{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_2gjj56egbplnwhgoowprlp7llbkzevtjql2mtkeiudeowfya5v3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 7 tests pass. Build succeeds. Summary:\n\n- **`cargo build`**: succeeds (warnings are in files I'm not allowed to modify — `src/lib.rs` crate name and unused imports/`mut` in `src/bin/`)\n- **`cargo test`**: all 7 tests pass\n  - `test_coding.rs`: `test_selftest`, `test_coding_encode`, `test_coding_decode`, `test_coding_roundtrip`, `test_error_single`, `test_error_double` — all ok\n  - `tests_log.rs`: `test_log2uint8` — ok\n\n### Implementation notes for `src/fast_hamming.rs`\n\nI replaced the five `unimplemented!()` stubs by porting `c_src/src/fast_hamming.c` to Rust:\n\n- **`log2uint8`** — `7 - x.leading_zeros() as u8` for nonzero input (matches `31 - __builtin_clz(v)` truncated to a `u8`).\n- **`hecc_encode_impl`** — Iterates 15 bytes × 8 bits, skipping Hamming parity positions (powers of two ≥ 4), accumulating `p1` (XOR of bit positions) and `p2` (overall parity). Pushes the 15 data bytes and a final byte composed of `p1 | (p2 << 7)`.\n- **`hecc_encode`** — Splits `input` into 15-byte blocks, calling the impl per block. For a partial trailing block, it zero-pads to 15, encodes, then truncates the appended data back to the original remainder length while keeping the parity byte.\n- **`hecc_decode_impl`** — Recomputes `p1`/`p2` and XORs against the stored check byte. If `p1 != 0`, factors in the overall parity; if both syndromes disagree it's a single-bit error and the impl flips the offending bit (using `log2uint8(p1)` to derive the data position). Returns `false` on detected double-bit errors.\n- **`hecc_decode`** — Rejects truncated lengths (`len % 16 == 1`), decodes 16-byte blocks, and for partial trailing blocks places the parity byte at index 15 of a zero-padded buffer so the impl reads it correctly, then trims to the actual data length. Returns `None` on any decode failure.\n\nHelper `parity_u8` replaces `__builtin_parity` for portability."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":27006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":999,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"803106ff-d56a-41f4-8be2-f42bf3ed0c1c","uuid":"ba6bb626-751f-492d-8a21-1a6fc8328c19"}
